--- math's sum, max and mean of a list holding an int past 64 bits: the modes
--- disagree.
---   interpreted: runtime error: line 14: a list of int is not a list of numbers
---   compiled:    1180591620717411300000, 1180591620717411300000, 590295810358705700000
--- Expected: one answer in both modes — the nearest float (sum[t] is a float, and
--- float[] of an int past 64 bits is the nearest float), or a refusal before the
--- program runs in both. The interpreter's words also mislead: a list of ints is
--- numbers. (Pushed onto `[]`, so not the open literal-list finding.)
use math

big = []
big = push[big, 2 ^ 70]
big = push[big, 1]
log[sum[big]]
log[max[big]]
log[mean[big]]
